{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428841-the-hisil-underworld-and-cosmology","id":428841,"title":"The Hisil, Underworld, and Cosmology","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T01:22:58-08:00","id":428841,"title":"The Hisil, Underworld, and Cosmology","content":"Alright. So I have a Fantasy/Sci-fi setting that I run games on. It takes cues from the <i>Witcher</i>, <i>Legacy of Kain</i>, and WoD, of course. The only splat that, so far, goes unchanged and fits are the Uratha. (Some 'in the past' changes, but werewolf society and how they work is remarkably resilient when transferring it to a fantasy realm.) Now, I'm thinking of simplifying it all to a Spectral Realm, and taking away Twilight. Ghosts or Spirits strong enough to use Reaching or in the presence of particular Conditions can do poltergeist activity, but when they cross over they automatically materialize (Ghosts can't Materialize, but can possess corpses). <br /> <br /> Now, what this has to do with the Uratha; how do the Uratha (assuming not much changes from the book) change if they are forced to deal with Ghosts and spirits of the dead more often? What if spirits of death are, usually, caught early and devoured by ghostly parasites (We'll call them slaugh, hungry ghosts that eat whatever Essence they can, becoming Magath of ghost/spirits)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T01:26:20-08:00","id":428858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428841-the-hisil-underworld-and-cosmology#post428841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, what this has to do with the Uratha; how do the Uratha (assuming not much changes from the book) change if they are forced to deal with Ghosts and spirits of the dead more often? What if spirits of death are, usually, caught early and devoured by ghostly parasites (We'll call them slaugh, hungry ghosts that eat whatever Essence they can, becoming Magath of ghost/spirits)</div> </div> </div> </div>So in short, cut out Sin-Eaters and allow the Uratha to take their place?<br /> <br /> And I think you mentioned how Giests get created as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T02:43:56-08:00","id":428892,"title":"","content":"Aye, it's one of the proposed ideas about how Geists are created. I'm thinking less 'archtypical' representation of Death and more... Hungry Ghosts, ala Exalted, instead instead of Blood, they eat Souls and Essence. Mainly becoming mindless scavengers and predators, unless they are especially strong-willed. (Perhaps those are Death lords?) Except, I'm porting over the Elder God of Legacy of Kain. He has Archons that are spirit creatures that eat souls and transfer it to the Elder god.<br /> <br /> I forsee Werewolves playing the same role, except that they will take Sin-Eater;s job, I suspect. Ghosts are rather rare, and most lost souls to end up descending into the Underworld which is, as you can imagine, the underground part of the Spectral Plane. Those who are not lost, fade into the Wheel of Fate, joining with a big background supernatural element, ala the Force, but Lost Souls... they need to be devoured to set them on the Wheel. Archons do that. Sluagh, however, I think are the 'lower souls' of humans, and split off becoming hungry for Essence. They gorge on spirits, or other ghosts, changing them.Then there are Vampire Wraiths, which are as it says on the tin, dead Vampires. Vampires do not pass onto the reincarnation, their spirits become something inbetween a ghost and a vampire. A nasty occurrence, and I assume one local Uratha are accustomed to fighting.<br /> <br /> The Sluagh from LoK are; <a href=\"http://legacyofkain.wikia.com/wiki/Sluagh_(family\" target=\"_blank\">http://legacyofkain.wikia.com/wiki/Sluagh_(family</a>)<br /> and some other creatures, <a href=\"http://legacyofkain.wikia.com/wiki/Legacy_of_Kain_Wiki:Nosgoth/Ghouls\" target=\"_blank\">http://legacyofkain.wikia.com/wiki/L...Nosgoth/Ghouls</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 03-05-2015, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}